{
  "notes": [
    "Part 1 agent eval set: 13 end-to-end scenarios.",
    "Ten of them anchor on the samples catalog by id instead of copying the task, the code and the tests, for the same reason the retrieval cases anchor on (material_id, heading) rather than on chunk ids: a copy rots silently the moment the catalog is edited, and a scenario that no longer matches the sample it was written for looks like an agent regression. The remaining three carry their bodies inline because they exercise outcomes no sample has — a solution that already passes, a mistake that needs no theory, and a statement carrying an injection.",
    "expected_tools is a list of ACCEPTABLE trajectories, not one golden path, and tool selection compares it as a multiset, so the order inside an alternative is not what that metric is about. The eight research plans shared by the technique cases are the ones a competent agent actually produces: search once, search twice with a refined query, search and then read the material in full, look at the topic list first, or read a material straight off the topic list without searching. The set was widened once already, after a real run took `list_material_topics -> get_learning_material` — a perfectly good plan the first draft had not thought of and would have scored as a failure. That is the failure mode this shape exists to make visible.",
    "expected_parameters constrains usability, never wording: which concept the query has to be about, that it is a question rather than a keyword, and that k is inside the tool's own bounds. A check on an exact query string would measure paraphrase.",
    "expected_outcome.mentions are synonym groups and the terms are stems: the hint has to hit at least one term from every group. They pin the concept the hint must land on, not a phrasing.",
    "expected_outcome.materials bounds what may be cited. It is a superset of the sample's own expected_material, because more than one note can legitimately fit a mistake — algo-loop-bounds and algo-parity-filters both speak to an inverted condition inside a loop."
  ],
